{"items":[{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-7vddpuvurhkbhcd3xa9xvp","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-7vddpuvurhkbhcd3xa9xvp","dateCreated":"2025-09-03T08:49:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-09-15T21:49:16+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus is now available in Asia Pacific (Jakarta), Asia Pacific (Hyderabad), Asia Pacific (Osaka), Asia Pacific (Melbourne), Asia Pacific (Taipei), Canada West (Calgary), Europe (Spain), Israel (Tel Aviv), Mexico (Central), Middle East (Bahrain), and US West (N. California). Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is a fully managed Prometheus-compatible monitoring service that makes it easy to monitor and alarm on operational metrics at scale.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe list of all supported regions where Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is generally available can be found in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/what-is-Amazon-Managed-Service-Prometheus.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e. Customers can send up to 1 billion active metrics to a single workspace and can create multiple workspaces per account, where a workspace is a logical space dedicated to the storage and querying of Prometheus metrics.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus, visit the user guide or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/prometheus/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/09/amazon-managed-service-prometheus-11-regions/","postDateTime":"2025-09-15T07:00:00Z","headline":"Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus now available in 11 additional AWS Regions"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-amp","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-amp","description":"general:products/amazon-amp","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-2e9ap1xf1rvazgyf69bu5d","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-2e9ap1xf1rvazgyf69bu5d","dateCreated":"2025-08-15T09:25:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-09-08T14:19:40+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus, a fully managed Prometheus-compatible monitoring service, now supports resource-based policies, making it easier to build applications that work across accounts. With resource-based policies, you can specify which Identity and Access Management (IAM) principals have access to ingest or query your Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus workspace.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo allow cross-account ingestion into an Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus workspace or query the metrics using PromQL from a different account, customers so far had to assume an IAM role in the workspace owner account. With this launch, you now can attach a resource-based policy to an Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus workspace and allow-list non-workspace owner to perform any actions using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/AMP-APIReference-Prometheus-Compatible-Apis.html\"\u003ePrometheus-compatible APIs\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis feature is now available in all regions where Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is generally available.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus collector, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/what-is-Amazon-Managed-Service-Prometheus.html\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/prometheus\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/08/amazon-managed-service-prometheus-resource-policies/","postDateTime":"2025-08-15T13:30:00.000Z","headline":"Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus adds support resource policies"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-amp","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-amp","description":"general:products/amazon-amp","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#d159149638","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"r9gVfGRj962apxPDMXch46","dateCreated":"2024-09-23T17:28:52+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-11-18T18:11:49+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus collector, a fully-managed agentless collector for Prometheus metrics, adds support for updating the scrape configuration inline and support for configuration via the Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus AWS console. Starting today, you can update collector parameters including scrape configuration as well as the destination Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus workspace. Further, you can view and edit collectors from within the Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus console.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nCustomers can now quickly iterate on the scrape configuration of Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus collectors. With this launch, customers can add, remove, and update scrape targets and jobs without downtime. In addition, you can now use the Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus AWS console to list, create, edit, and delete collectors.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus collector is available in all regions where Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is available. To learn more about Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus collector, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/AMP-collector-how-to.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/prometheus\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/11/amazon-managed-service-prometheus-collector-support-update-aws-console","postDateTime":"2024-11-18T13:00:00-04:00","contentType":"launch announcement","headline":"Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus collector adds support for update and AWS console"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-amp","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-amp","description":"general:products/amazon-amp","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-09-17T18:03:36+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2024-05-amazon-managed-service-prometheus-inline-editing","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/05/amazon-managed-service-prometheus-inline-editing/","dateCreated":"2024-05-16T18:43:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:00:35+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus now supports inline editing of rules and alert manager configuration directly from the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS console\u003c/a\u003e. Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is a fully managed Prometheus-compatible monitoring service that makes it easy to monitor and alarm on operational metrics at scale. Prometheus is a popular Cloud Native Computing Foundation open-source project for monitoring and alerting on metrics from compute environments such as \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/eks/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Elastic Kubernetes Service\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003ePreviously, customers could define alerting and recording rules, or alert manager definition, by importing respective configuration defined in a YAML file, via the AWS console. Now, they can import, preview, and edit existing rules or alert manager configurations from YAML files or create them directly from the AWS console. The inline editing experience allows customers to preview their rules and alert manager configuration prior to setting them.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis feature is now available in all regions where Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/what-is-Amazon-Managed-Service-Prometheus.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003egenerally available\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/prometheus/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/prometheus/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003epricing page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-05-16T18:42:44Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/05/amazon-managed-service-prometheus-inline-editing/","postDateTime":"2024-05-16T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus now supports inline editing of alert manager and rules configuration","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus now supports inline editing of rules and alert manager configuration directly from the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS console\u003c/a\u003e. Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is a fully managed Prometheus-compatible monitoring service that makes it easy to monitor and alarm on operational metrics at scale. Prometheus is a popular Cloud Native Computing Foundation open-source project for monitoring and alerting on metrics from compute environments such as \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/eks.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Elastic Kubernetes Service\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-amp","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-amp","description":"general:products/amazon-amp","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2024-05-amazon-managed-service-prometheus-collector-eks-access-management-controls","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/05/amazon-managed-service-prometheus-collector-eks-access-management-controls/","dateCreated":"2024-05-10T17:18:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:05:29+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus collector, a fully-managed agentless collector for Prometheus metrics now integrates with the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/access-entries.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EKS access management controls\u003c/a\u003e. Starting today, the collector utilizes the EKS access management controls to create a managed access policy that allows the collector to discover and collect Prometheus metrics.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus collector with support for EKS access management controls is available in all regions where Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is available. To learn more about Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus collector, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/AMP-collector.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/prometheus/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-05-10T17:17:50Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/05/amazon-managed-service-prometheus-collector-eks-access-management-controls/","postDateTime":"2024-05-10T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus collector integrates with Amazon EKS access management controls","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus collector, a fully-managed agentless collector for Prometheus metrics now integrates with the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/access-entries.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EKS access management controls\u003c/a\u003e. Starting today, the collector utilizes the EKS access management controls to create a managed access policy that allows the collector to discover and collect Prometheus metrics.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-amp","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-amp","description":"general:products/amazon-amp","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#containers","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"containers","description":"marketing:marchitecture/containers","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-eks","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-eks","description":"general:products/amazon-eks","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:52:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:52:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2024-03-amazon-managed-service-prometheus-collector-cloudformation","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/03/amazon-managed-service-prometheus-collector-cloudformation/","dateCreated":"2024-03-29T17:59:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:02:12+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus collector, a fully-managed agentless collector for Prometheus metrics from Amazon EKS workloads, now supports AWS CloudFormation. Starting today, you can easily create, configure, and manage Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus collectors using CloudFormation templates. With AWS CloudFormation, you can use a programming language or simple text file to automatically configure collectors for Prometheus metrics from Amazon EKS infrastructure and applications. You can also continue utilizing the Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus collector using the AWS Management Console, Command Line Interface (CLI) or API.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus collector is available in all regions where Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is available. To learn more about Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus collector, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/AMP-collector.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/prometheus/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-03-29T17:59:25Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/03/amazon-managed-service-prometheus-collector-cloudformation/","postDateTime":"2024-03-29T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus collector now supports CloudFormation","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus collector, a fully-managed agentless collector for Prometheus metrics from Amazon EKS workloads, now supports AWS CloudFormation. Starting today, you can easily create, configure, and manage Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus collectors using CloudFormation templates. With AWS CloudFormation, you can use a programming language or simple text file to automatically configure collectors for Prometheus metrics from Amazon EKS infrastructure and applications. You can also continue utilizing the Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus collector using the AWS Management Console, Command Line Interface (CLI) or API.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#containers","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"containers","description":"marketing:marchitecture/containers","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-amp","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-amp","description":"general:products/amazon-amp","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-cloudformation","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-cloudformation","description":"general:products/aws-cloudformation","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-12-amazon-managed-service-prometheus-kms-keys","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/12/amazon-managed-service-prometheus-kms-keys/","dateCreated":"2023-12-21T22:46:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:52:00+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now use customer managed keys defined in AWS Key Management Service to encrypt data residing in their Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus workspaces. Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is a fully managed Prometheus-compatible monitoring service that makes it easy to monitor and alarm on operational metrics at scale. Prometheus is a popular Cloud Native Computing Foundation open-source project for monitoring and alerting on metrics from compute environments such as \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/eks/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Elastic Kubernetes Service\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus has always provided encryption by default using AWS owned KMS keys for all data stored by the service. This feature provides you the option of adding a self-managed security layer to help you meet the compliance and regulatory requirements of your organization.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis feature is now available in all regions where the Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is available. To get started, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/prometheus/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e for more information.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-12-21T22:46:24Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/12/amazon-managed-service-prometheus-kms-keys/","postDateTime":"2023-12-21T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus now supports customer managed KMS keys","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now use customer managed keys defined in AWS Key Management Service to encrypt data residing in their Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus workspaces. Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is a fully managed Prometheus-compatible monitoring service that makes it easy to monitor and alarm on operational metrics at scale. Prometheus is a popular Cloud Native Computing Foundation open-source project for monitoring and alerting on metrics from compute environments such as \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/eks.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Elastic Kubernetes Service\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#containers","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"containers","description":"marketing:marchitecture/containers","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-amp","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-amp","description":"general:products/amazon-amp","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-11-amazon-managed-service-prometheus-agentless-collector-metrics-eks","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/11/amazon-managed-service-prometheus-agentless-collector-metrics-eks/","dateCreated":"2023-11-26T20:18:34+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:40:01+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eWe are excited to announce Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus collector, a fully-managed agentless collector customers can use to collect Prometheus metrics from their workloads running on Amazon EKS. Customers can now enable the discovery and collection of Prometheus metrics from their Amazon EKS applications and infrastructure through the EKS console or through an API call, without having to self-manage agents.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eCustomers currently invest days, if not weeks, of effort to monitor, right-size, and operate Prometheus agents. Now with Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus collector, customers can automatically discover and collect Prometheus metrics from their Amazon EKS applications, infrastructure, and the Kubernetes apiserver without having to install any agents in their cluster. The fully-managed collector removes the “undifferentiated heavy lifting” of installing, patching, scaling, and upgrading agents for the discovery and collection of Prometheus metrics. The collector provides customers with a multi-AZ, highly available, reliable, and fully-managed service for collecting Prometheus metrics without any data ever leaving secure VPCs.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, customers can utilize the Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus APIs, SDK, CLI and the Amazon EKS console to create fully-managed collectors. Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus collector is available in all regions where Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is available. To learn more about Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus collector, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/AMP-collector.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/prometheus/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-11-26T20:18:25Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/11/amazon-managed-service-prometheus-agentless-collector-metrics-eks/","postDateTime":"2023-11-26T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus launches an agentless collector for Prometheus metrics from Amazon EKS","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eWe are excited to announce Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus collector, a fully-managed agentless collector customers can use to collect Prometheus metrics from their workloads running on Amazon EKS. Customers can now enable the discovery and collection of Prometheus metrics from their Amazon EKS applications and infrastructure through the EKS console or through an API call, without having to self-manage agents.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-eks","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-eks","description":"general:products/amazon-eks","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:52:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:52:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-amp","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-amp","description":"general:products/amazon-amp","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#containers","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"containers","description":"marketing:marchitecture/containers","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-11-amazon-managed-grafana-community-plugins","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/11/amazon-managed-grafana-community-plugins/","dateCreated":"2023-11-15T21:05:45+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:03:44+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Grafana now features a new self-service plugin management experience for Grafana community plugins. With this release, Amazon Managed Grafana administrators can discover and install Grafana community plugins directly from their workspace. Plugins enable you to extend your Grafana experience, unifying data from a wider variety of data sources with visualizations tailored to analyze your unique datasets.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith this release, Amazon Managed Grafana workspace administrators can discover and install plugins from over 300 pre-built Grafana community plugins, to visualize data from their disparate data sources in a single view. You can now glean insights across Amazon services such as Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus, Amazon CloudWatch, right next to third party applications such as Apache Cassandra, PagerDuty or databases such as Redis, Vertica, with visualization panels best suited to represent your data.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe new self-service plugin management experience is supported on all Amazon Managed Grafana workspaces with Grafana version 9.4, across all AWS regions where Amazon Managed Grafana is \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/grafana/latest/userguide/what-is-Amazon-Managed-Service-Grafana.html#AMG-supported-Regions\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003egenerally available\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eYou can enable self-service plugin management for your Amazon Managed Grafana workspace from the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/grafana/home/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Console\u003c/a\u003e, SDK, or CLI. Check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/grafana/latest/userguide/grafana-plugins.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Managed Grafana user guide\u003c/a\u003e for detailed documentation. To learn more about Amazon Managed Grafana, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/grafana/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/grafana/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003epricing page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-11-15T21:05:33Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/11/amazon-managed-grafana-community-plugins/","postDateTime":"2023-11-15T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Extend your Amazon Managed Grafana experience with Grafana community plugins","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Grafana now features a new self-service plugin management experience for Grafana community plugins. With this release, Amazon Managed Grafana administrators can discover and install Grafana community plugins directly from their workspace. Plugins enable you to extend your Grafana experience, unifying data from a wider variety of data sources with visualizations tailored to analyze your unique datasets.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-amp","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-amp","description":"general:products/amazon-amp","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-managed-service-for-grafana","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-managed-service-for-grafana","description":"general:products/amazon-managed-service-for-grafana","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:41:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:41:27+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-05-amazon-managed-services-prometheus-4-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/05/amazon-managed-services-prometheus-4-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T15:00:37+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:43:02+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus is now available in Asia Pacific (Mumbai), Asia Pacific (Seoul), South America (Sao Paulo) and Europe (Paris). Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is a fully managed Prometheus-compatible monitoring service that makes it easy to monitor and alarm on operational metrics at scale. Prometheus is a popular Cloud Native Computing Foundation open-source project for monitoring and alerting that is optimized for container environments such as Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe list of all supported regions where Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is generally available can be found on the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/what-is-Amazon-Managed-Service-Prometheus.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e. Customers can send up to 500 million active metrics to a single workspace and can create many workspaces per account, enabling the storage and analysis of billions of Prometheus metrics. A workspace is a logical space dedicated to the storage and querying of Prometheus metrics. To get started, check out the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/prometheus/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/prometheus/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003epricing page\u003c/a\u003e for more information.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-05-09T18:48:01Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/05/amazon-managed-services-prometheus-4-regions/","postDateTime":"2023-05-09T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus now available in 4 additional AWS regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus is now available in Asia Pacific (Mumbai), Asia Pacific (Seoul), South America (Sao Paulo) and Europe (Paris). Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is a fully managed Prometheus-compatible monitoring service that makes it easy to monitor and alarm on operational metrics at scale. Prometheus is a popular Cloud Native Computing Foundation open-source project for monitoring and alerting that is optimized for container environments such as Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#containers","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"containers","description":"marketing:marchitecture/containers","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-amp","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-amp","description":"general:products/amazon-amp","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-03-amazon-managed-service-prometheus-500m-metrics-workspace","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/03/amazon-managed-service-prometheus-500m-metrics-workspace/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:48:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:41:16+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus is a fully managed Prometheus-compatible service that monitors and provides alerts on containerized applications and infrastructure at scale. Prometheus is a Cloud Native Computing Foundation open source project for monitoring and alerting that is optimized for container environments such as Amazon EKS and Amazon ECS. With this release, customers can send up to 500M active metrics to a single workspace after filing a service limit increase request, and can create many workspaces per account, enabling the storage and analysis of billions of Prometheus metrics. To get started, customers can create an \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/CW-logs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus workspace\u003c/a\u003e and increase their workspace active series limits by filing a service limit increase request in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/support/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Support Center\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/servicequotas/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Quotas\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e500M active metrics workspaces are available in every region where Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is generally available. Get started with Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus by checking out our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/CW-logs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-03-31T17:06:20Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/03/amazon-managed-service-prometheus-500m-metrics-workspace/","postDateTime":"2023-03-31T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus supports 500M active metrics per workspace","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus is a fully managed Prometheus-compatible service that monitors and provides alerts on containerized applications and infrastructure at scale. Prometheus is a Cloud Native Computing Foundation open source project for monitoring and alerting that is optimized for container environments such as Amazon EKS and Amazon ECS. With this release, customers can send up to 500M active metrics to a single workspace after filing a service limit increase request, and can create many workspaces per account, enabling the storage and analysis of billions of Prometheus metrics. To get started, customers can create an \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/CW-logs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus workspace\u003c/a\u003e and increase their workspace active series limits by filing a service limit increase request in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/support/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Support Center\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/servicequotas/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Quotas\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-amp","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-amp","description":"general:products/amazon-amp","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-12-amazon-managed-services-prometheus-vpc-endpoint-policies","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/12/amazon-managed-services-prometheus-vpc-endpoint-policies/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:57:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:31:23+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/what-is-Amazon-Managed-Service-Prometheus.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus\u003c/a\u003e now supports \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/vpc-endpoints-access.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eVPC endpoint policies\u003c/a\u003e configured using Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (Amazon VPC). Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is a fully managed Prometheus-compatible monitoring service that monitors and alarms on operational metrics at scale. It does this without you having to manage the underlying infrastructure required to scale and secure the ingestion, storage, alerting, and querying of metrics. With this feature, customers can now configure VPC endpoint policies in the Amazon VPC console, via Command Line Interface or SDK, or through AWS CloudFormation. These policies can restrict access of Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus endpoints to particular AWS accounts, IAM users, and IAM roles.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eVPC Endpoint policies created can be applied to Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus workspaces in every region where Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is generally available. Get started by checking out our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/AMP-and-interface-VPC.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-12-19T18:01:09Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/12/amazon-managed-services-prometheus-vpc-endpoint-policies/","postDateTime":"2022-12-19T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus now supports VPC endpoint policies","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/what-is-Amazon-Managed-Service-Prometheus.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus\u003c/a\u003e now supports \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/vpc-endpoints-access.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eVPC endpoint policies\u003c/a\u003e configured using Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (Amazon VPC). Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is a fully managed Prometheus-compatible monitoring service that monitors and alarms on operational metrics at scale. It does this without you having to manage the underlying infrastructure required to scale and secure the ingestion, storage, alerting, and querying of metrics. With this feature, customers can now configure VPC endpoint policies in the Amazon VPC console, via Command Line Interface or SDK, or through AWS CloudFormation. These policies can restrict access of Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus endpoints to particular AWS accounts, IAM users, and IAM roles.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#containers","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"containers","description":"marketing:marchitecture/containers","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-amp","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-amp","description":"general:products/amazon-amp","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-11-amazon-managed-grafana-visualizing-prometheus-alertmanager-rules-configuration-apis","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/amazon-managed-grafana-visualizing-prometheus-alertmanager-rules-configuration-apis/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:41:50+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:33:59+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/grafana/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Managed Grafana\u003c/a\u003e now supports visualizing Prometheus Alertmanager rules, new configuration APIs and additional visualization plugins. AWS customers using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/prometheus/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus\u003c/a\u003e, or running self-managed Prometheus environments can visualize and analyze their Alertmanager rules, alert states, silences and contact points directly in an Amazon Managed Grafana workspace. Customers can opt-in to viewing their Prometheus Alertmanager rules by turning on Grafana alerting from the Amazon Managed Grafana console or programmatically using the new configuration APIs, designed to manage workspace settings. Current workspace configuration details can be retrieved using the DescribeWorkspaceConfiguration API and settings can be updated via the UpdateWorkspaceConfiguration API. The CreateWorkspace API, used to programmatically create, delete and manage Grafana workspaces, has been updated to allow customers to enable Grafana alerting during workspace creation. Amazon Managed Grafana also adds support for Sankey, Plotly and Scatter visualization plugins, providing customers more visualization options for their dashboards.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Grafana is a fully managed service that takes care of the provisioning, setup, scaling, and maintenance of Grafana servers. Grafana alerting is available in every region where Amazon Managed Grafana is generally available. To get started with Grafana alerting for visualizing Prometheus Alertmanager rules, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/grafana/home/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Managed Grafana Console\u003c/a\u003e or check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/grafana/latest/userguide/alerts-overview.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Managed Grafana user guide\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/grafana/latest/APIReference/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAPI Reference\u003c/a\u003e, or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/reference/grafana/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eCLI reference\u003c/a\u003e for detailed documentation.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-11-23T22:03:41Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/amazon-managed-grafana-visualizing-prometheus-alertmanager-rules-configuration-apis/","postDateTime":"2022-11-23T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Managed Grafana now supports visualizing Prometheus Alertmanager rules and new configuration APIs","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/grafana.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Managed Grafana\u003c/a\u003e now supports visualizing Prometheus Alertmanager rules, new configuration APIs and additional visualization plugins. AWS customers using \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/prometheus.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus\u003c/a\u003e, or running self-managed Prometheus environments can visualize and analyze their Alertmanager rules, alert states, silences and contact points directly in an Amazon Managed Grafana workspace. Customers can opt-in to viewing their Prometheus Alertmanager rules by turning on Grafana alerting from the Amazon Managed Grafana console or programmatically using the new configuration APIs, designed to manage workspace settings. Current workspace configuration details can be retrieved using the DescribeWorkspaceConfiguration API and settings can be updated via the UpdateWorkspaceConfiguration API. The CreateWorkspace API, used to programmatically create, delete and manage Grafana workspaces, has been updated to allow customers to enable Grafana alerting during workspace creation. Amazon Managed Grafana also adds support for Sankey, Plotly and Scatter visualization plugins, providing customers more visualization options for their dashboards.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-managed-service-for-grafana","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-managed-service-for-grafana","description":"general:products/amazon-managed-service-for-grafana","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:41:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:41:27+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-amp","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-amp","description":"general:products/amazon-amp","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-11-amazon-managed-service-prometheus-200m-active-metrics-workspace","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/amazon-managed-service-prometheus-200m-active-metrics-workspace/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:41:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:45:04+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus now supports 200M active metrics per workspace. Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is a fully managed Prometheus-compatible monitoring service that makes it easy to monitor and alarm on operational metrics at scale. Prometheus is a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.cncf.io/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eCloud Native Computing Foundation\u003c/a\u003e open source project for monitoring and alerting that is optimized for container environments such as Amazon EKS and Amazon ECS. With this release, customers can send up to 200M active metrics to a single workspace after filing a limit increase, and can create many workspaces per account, enabling the storage and analysis of billions of Prometheus metrics. To get started, customers can create an \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/CW-logs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus workspace\u003c/a\u003e and increase their workspace active series limits by filing a limit increase in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/support/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Support Center\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/servicequotas/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Quotas\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e200M active metrics workspaces are available in every region where Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is generally available. Get started with Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus by checking out our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/what-is-Amazon-Managed-Service-Prometheus.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-11-15T19:40:58Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/amazon-managed-service-prometheus-200m-active-metrics-workspace/","postDateTime":"2022-11-15T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus supports 200M active metrics per workspace","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus now supports 200M active metrics per workspace. Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is a fully managed Prometheus-compatible monitoring service that makes it easy to monitor and alarm on operational metrics at scale. Prometheus is a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.cncf.io/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eCloud Native Computing Foundation\u003c/a\u003e open source project for monitoring and alerting that is optimized for container environments such as Amazon EKS and Amazon ECS. With this release, customers can send up to 200M active metrics to a single workspace after filing a limit increase, and can create many workspaces per account, enabling the storage and analysis of billions of Prometheus metrics. To get started, customers can create an \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/CW-logs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus workspace\u003c/a\u003e and increase their workspace active series limits by filing a limit increase in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/support/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Support Center\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/servicequotas/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Quotas\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-amp","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-amp","description":"general:products/amazon-amp","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-09-amazon-managed-service-prometheus-alert-manager-ruler-logs-available-amazon-cloudwatch-logs","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/09/amazon-managed-service-prometheus-alert-manager-ruler-logs-available-amazon-cloudwatch-logs/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:51:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:18:34+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus now provides Alert Manager \u0026amp; Ruler logs to help customers troubleshoot their alerting pipeline and configuration in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/WhatIsCloudWatchLogs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon CloudWatch Logs\u003c/a\u003e. Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is a fully managed Prometheus-compatible monitoring service that makes it easy to monitor and alarm on operational metrics at scale. Prometheus is a popular \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.cncf.io/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eCloud Native Computing Foundation\u003c/a\u003e open source project for monitoring and alerting that is optimized for container environments. The Alert Manager allows customers to group, route, deduplicate, and silence alarms before routing them to end users via Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS). The Ruler allows customers to define recording and alerting rules, which are queries that are evaluated at regular intervals. With Alert Manager and Ruler logs, customers can troubleshoot issues in their alerting pipelines including missing Amazon SNS topic permissions, misconfigured alert manager routes, and rules that fail to execute.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAlert Manager and Ruler logs are now generally available in all regions where Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is available. Please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/cloudwatch/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon CloudWatch pricing page\u003c/a\u003e to learn more about logs pricing. Get started with Alert Manager and Ruler logs by checking out our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/CW-logs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-09-02T17:54:29Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/09/amazon-managed-service-prometheus-alert-manager-ruler-logs-available-amazon-cloudwatch-logs/","postDateTime":"2022-09-02T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus Alert Manager \u0026 Ruler logs now available in Amazon CloudWatch Logs","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus now provides Alert Manager \u0026amp; Ruler logs to help customers troubleshoot their alerting pipeline and configuration in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/WhatIsCloudWatchLogs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon CloudWatch Logs\u003c/a\u003e. Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is a fully managed Prometheus-compatible monitoring service that makes it easy to monitor and alarm on operational metrics at scale. Prometheus is a popular \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.cncf.io/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eCloud Native Computing Foundation\u003c/a\u003e open source project for monitoring and alerting that is optimized for container environments. The Alert Manager allows customers to group, route, deduplicate, and silence alarms before routing them to end users via Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS). The Ruler allows customers to define recording and alerting rules, which are queries that are evaluated at regular intervals. With Alert Manager and Ruler logs, customers can troubleshoot issues in their alerting pipelines including missing Amazon SNS topic permissions, misconfigured alert manager routes, and rules that fail to execute.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#containers","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"containers","description":"marketing:marchitecture/containers","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-amp","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-amp","description":"general:products/amazon-amp","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-cloudwatch-logs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-cloudwatch-logs","description":"general:products/amazon-cloudwatch-logs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:30+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:30+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-05-monitor-amazon-managed-service-prometheus-usage-amazon-cloudwatch-usage-metrics","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/05/monitor-amazon-managed-service-prometheus-usage-amazon-cloudwatch-usage-metrics/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:39:45+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:11:12+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus usage metrics are now available in Amazon CloudWatch at no additional charge. Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is a fully managed Prometheus-compatible monitoring service that makes it easy to monitor and alarm on operational metrics at scale. Prometheus is a popular \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.cncf.io/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eCloud Native Computing Foundation\u003c/a\u003e open-source project for monitoring and alerting that is optimized for container environments. With \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/CloudWatch-Usage-Metrics.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon CloudWatch usage metrics\u003c/a\u003e, you can check your Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus workspace usage, and can start to proactively manage your quotas.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus is generally available in the following regions: US East (Ohio), US East (N. Virginia), US West (Oregon), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), Europe (Frankfurt), Europe (Ireland), Europe (Stockholm), and Europe (London) Regions. To get started with usage metrics, check out our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/what-is-Amazon-Managed-Service-Prometheus.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e on Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus’s CloudWatch usage metrics.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-05-09T17:53:00Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/05/monitor-amazon-managed-service-prometheus-usage-amazon-cloudwatch-usage-metrics/","postDateTime":"2022-05-09T04:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Monitor your Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus usage with Amazon CloudWatch usage metrics","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus usage metrics are now available in Amazon CloudWatch at no additional charge. Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is a fully managed Prometheus-compatible monitoring service that makes it easy to monitor and alarm on operational metrics at scale. Prometheus is a popular \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.cncf.io/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eCloud Native Computing Foundation\u003c/a\u003e open-source project for monitoring and alerting that is optimized for container environments. With \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/CloudWatch-Usage-Metrics.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon CloudWatch usage metrics\u003c/a\u003e, you can check your Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus workspace usage, and can start to proactively manage your quotas.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#containers","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"containers","description":"marketing:marchitecture/containers","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-eks","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-eks","description":"general:products/amazon-eks","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:52:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:52:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-amp","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-amp","description":"general:products/amazon-amp","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-ecs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-ecs","description":"general:products/amazon-ecs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-05-amazon-managed-service-prometheus-now-available-europe-london-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/05/amazon-managed-service-prometheus-now-available-europe-london-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:52:56+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:18:56+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus is now available in Europe (London) Region. Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is a fully managed Prometheus-compatible monitoring service that makes it easy to monitor and alarm on operational metrics at scale. Prometheus is a popular Cloud Native Computing Foundation open-source project for monitoring and alerting that is optimized for container environments.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus is now generally available in the following regions: US East (Ohio), US East (N. Virginia), US West (Oregon), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), Europe (Frankfurt), Europe (Ireland), Europe (Stockholm), and Europe (London) Regions. To get started, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/what-is-Amazon-Managed-Service-Prometheus.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/prometheus/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/prometheus/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003epricing page\u003c/a\u003e for more information.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-05-04T21:22:57Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/05/amazon-managed-service-prometheus-now-available-europe-london-region/","postDateTime":"2022-05-04T04:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is now available in Europe (London) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus is now available in Europe (London) Region. Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is a fully managed Prometheus-compatible monitoring service that makes it easy to monitor and alarm on operational metrics at scale. Prometheus is a popular Cloud Native Computing Foundation open-source project for monitoring and alerting that is optimized for container environments.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-ecs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-ecs","description":"general:products/amazon-ecs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-amp","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-amp","description":"general:products/amazon-amp","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-eks","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-eks","description":"general:products/amazon-eks","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:52:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:52:19+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-04-eks-opentelemetry-operator-now-available","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/04/eks-opentelemetry-operator-now-available/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:36:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:39:25+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) now supports using the Amazon EKS console, AWS Command Line Interface (CLI), and EKS API to install and manage the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/otel/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Distro for OpenTelemetry\u003c/a\u003e (ADOT) Operator. This launch enables a simplified experience for instrumenting your applications running on Amazon EKS to send metrics and traces to multiple monitoring services including \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/xray/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS X-Ray\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/prometheus/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus\u003c/a\u003e, and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/cloudwatch/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon CloudWatch\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eADOT is designed as a secure, production-ready, AWS-supported distribution of the OpenTelemetry project, which provides open source APIs, libraries, and agents to collect distributed traces and metrics for application and cluster infrastructure monitoring. The ADOT Operator is an implementation of the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/extend-kubernetes/operator/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eKubernetes Operator\u003c/a\u003e. The ADOT Operator manages collection agents that receive, process, and export telemetry data in multiple data formats to open source and vendor-service backends. With this launch, the ADOT Operator can now be installed, managed, and updated directly through the EKS Console, AWS CLI and EKS API. You can see available add-ons and compatible versions in the EKS API, select the version of the add-on you want to run on your cluster, and configure key settings such as the IAM role used by the add-on when it runs. Using EKS add-ons you can go from cluster creation to running applications in a single command and easily keep tooling in your cluster up to date.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more and get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/eks-add-ons.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EKS documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp; \u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-04-21T22:14:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/04/eks-opentelemetry-operator-now-available/","postDateTime":"2022-04-21T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"EKS add-ons support for the OpenTelemetry Operator is now generally available","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) now supports using the Amazon EKS console, AWS Command Line Interface (CLI), and EKS API to install and manage the \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/otel.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Distro for OpenTelemetry\u003c/a\u003e (ADOT) Operator. This launch enables a simplified experience for instrumenting your applications running on Amazon EKS to send metrics and traces to multiple monitoring services including \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/xray.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS X-Ray\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/prometheus.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus\u003c/a\u003e, and \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/cloudwatch.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon CloudWatch\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-cloudwatch","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-cloudwatch","description":"general:products/amazon-cloudwatch","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:47+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-amp","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-amp","description":"general:products/amazon-amp","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#containers","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"containers","description":"marketing:marchitecture/containers","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-09-amazon-managed-service-prometheus-alert-manager-rules","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/09/amazon-managed-service-prometheus-alert-manager-rules/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:42:29+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:47:49+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus is now generally available. Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is a fully managed Prometheus-compatible monitoring service that makes it easy to monitor and alarm on operational metrics at scale. Prometheus is a popular Cloud Native Computing Foundation open-source project for monitoring and alerting that is optimized for container environments.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAs part of this launch, we are introducing additional capabilities such as the Prometheus-compatible alert manager, recording rules and alerting rules. We also added support for provisioning Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus workspaces, rules configurations, and alert manager configurations with AWS CloudFormation. You can track and audit changes made to your Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus workspaces with an expanded set of CloudTrail logs, such as when recording rules are deleted, alert configurations are changed, and more. Customers can also tag their Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus workspaces to help manage, identify, organize, filter, and control access to them.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus is generally available in the following regions: US East (Ohio), US East (N. Virginia), US West (Oregon), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), Europe (Frankfurt), Europe (Ireland), and Europe (Stockholm). To get started, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/what-is-Amazon-Managed-Service-Prometheus.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/amazon-managed-service-for-prometheus-is-now-generally-available-with-alert-manager-and-ruler\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS News Blog\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, visit the Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/prometheus/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/prometheus/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003epricing page\u003c/a\u003e for more information.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-09-29T21:11:38Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/09/amazon-managed-service-prometheus-alert-manager-rules/","postDateTime":"2021-09-29T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is now Generally Available with support for alert manager and rules","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus is now generally available. Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus is a fully managed Prometheus-compatible monitoring service that makes it easy to monitor and alarm on operational metrics at scale. Prometheus is a popular Cloud Native Computing Foundation open-source project for monitoring and alerting that is optimized for container environments.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-cloudformation","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-cloudformation","description":"general:products/aws-cloudformation","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-amp","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-amp","description":"general:products/amazon-amp","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#containers","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"containers","description":"marketing:marchitecture/containers","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-05-aws-announces-a-price-reduction-for-amazon-managed-service-for-prometheus-amp","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/05/aws-announces-a-price-reduction-for-amazon-managed-service-for-prometheus-amp/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:27:06+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:16:54+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, we are reducing the price of metric samples ingested by up to 84% for Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus (AMP). Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus (AMP) is a fully managed Prometheus-compatible monitoring service that makes it easy to monitor containerized applications at scale. With AMP, you can use the open source Prometheus Query Language (PromQL) to monitor the performance of containerized workloads on AWS or on-premises. AMP automatically scales the ingestion, storage, and querying of operational metrics (from, for example, your Amazon Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) clusters) as workloads grow or shrink, and is integrated with AWS security services such as AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM), AWS PrivateLink, and AWS CloudTrail to enable fast and secure access to data.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith AMP, you pay only for what you use, based on metric samples ingested, metrics and metric samples stored, and query execution time. We are reducing the current price of metric samples ingested depending on volume. The new pricing is as follows:\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e$0.90 per 10M samples ingested for the first 2 billion samples\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e$0.35 per 10M samples ingested for the next 250 billion samples\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e$0.16 per 10M samples ingested for anything over 252 billion samples (cumulative sum of previous 2 tiers)\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more details on the new AMP pricing for all supported regions, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/prometheus/pricing/\"\u003eAMP Pricing page\u003c/a\u003e. These pricing changes are applicable in all currently \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/what-is-Amazon-Managed-Service-Prometheus.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003esupported regions\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;in which AMP is currently available. Reduction in pricing for existing AMP customers will be done automatically effective May 4, 2021. To learn more, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/prometheus/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAMP page\u003c/a\u003e, or get started with the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/AMP-getting-started.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAMP documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-05-04T21:18:36Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/05/aws-announces-a-price-reduction-for-amazon-managed-service-for-prometheus-amp/","postDateTime":"2021-05-04T14:45:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS announces a price reduction for Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus (AMP)","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday, we are reducing the price of metric samples ingested by up to 84% for Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus (AMP). Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus (AMP) is a fully managed Prometheus-compatible monitoring service that makes it easy to monitor containerized applications at scale. With AMP, you can use the open source Prometheus Query Language (PromQL) to monitor the performance of containerized workloads on AWS or on-premises. AMP automatically scales the ingestion, storage, and querying of operational metrics (from, for example, your Amazon Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) clusters) as workloads grow or shrink, and is integrated with AWS security services such as AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM), AWS PrivateLink, and AWS CloudTrail to enable fast and secure access to data.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#containers","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"containers","description":"marketing:marchitecture/containers","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-amp","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-amp","description":"general:products/amazon-amp","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-eks","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-eks","description":"general:products/amazon-eks","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:52:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:52:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-ecs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-ecs","description":"general:products/amazon-ecs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-12-aws-announces-amazon-managed-service-for-prometheus","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/12/aws-announces-amazon-managed-service-for-prometheus/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:10+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:08:23+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus (AMP) is a new, fully managed Prometheus-compatible monitoring service that makes it easy to monitor containerized applications at scale. The Cloud Native Computing Foundation’s Prometheus project is a popular open source and alerting monitoring solution optimized for container environments. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus, you can use the open source Prometheus Query Language (PromQL) to monitor the performance of containerized workloads on AWS or on-premises, without having to manage the underlying infrastructure for scalability, availability, and security. AMP automatically scales the ingestion, storage, and querying of operational metrics (from, for example, your Kubernetes clusters) as workloads grow or shrink, and is integrated with AWS security services such as AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM), AWS PrivateLink, and  AWS CloudTrail to enable fast and secure access to data. The service is also integrated with Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS), Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS), and AWS Distro for OpenTelemetry.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus is available in preview in US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), EU (Frankfurt), and EU (Ireland). See the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/prometheus/\"\u003eproduct overview page\u003c/a\u003e for more information and to get started.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-12-15T18:19:34Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/12/aws-announces-amazon-managed-service-for-prometheus/","postDateTime":"2020-12-15T12:42:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS announces Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus for container monitoring","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Managed Service for Prometheus (AMP) is a new, fully managed Prometheus-compatible monitoring service that makes it easy to monitor containerized applications at scale. The Cloud Native Computing Foundation’s Prometheus project is a popular open source and alerting monitoring solution optimized for container environments. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#reinvent-2020-werner","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"reinvent-2020-werner","description":"marketing:marchitecture/reinvent-2020-werner","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-amp","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-amp","description":"general:products/amazon-amp","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:02:07+0000"}]}],"metadata":{"count":21,"totalHits":21},"fieldTypes":{"regionalAvailability":"LongText","nofollow":"Boolean","date":"Date","language":"Text","title":"Text","postDateTime":"DateTime","body":"Text","postSummary":"LongText","ctaLabel":"Text","mediaThumbnail":"Text","nosnippet":"Boolean","price":"Text","ctaLink":"URL","headline":"Text","contentType":"Text","bodyBack":"LongText","secondaryCTALabel":"Text","primaryCTALink":"URL","noindex":"Boolean","level":"Text","heading":"Text","mediaType":"Text","mediaAlt":"Text","headlineUrl":"Text","mediaSrc":"URL","durationMinutes":"Number","badge":"JSON","videoImageUrl":"URL","postBody":"LongText","secondaryCTALink":"URL","Video":"URL","modifiedDate":"DateTime","namePerson":"Text","location":"Text","time":"Text","publishedDate":"DateTime","durationReadtime":"Number","primaryCTALabel":"Text"}}